This is a .zip of a Moun River workspace featuring the 1st set of CanHobby Examples for the peripherals in the CH32V003

Download and unzip into a separate directory then open that directory as a workspace in the Moun River Studio IDE.
this 1st set features:

- UART - printf output, Interrupt driven input with a Menu as example.
- SysClk - confiured to Max 48 MHz.
- ChipID with full example to show the Chip version.
- Timer blinking an LED with the Base Frequency controlled from the Menu.
- SisTick blinking an LED with the Base Frequency controlled from the Menu.

